      "content": "I understand your frustration, and I apologize for the excessive goblin metaphors earlier. That was a mistake on my part; I should have focused on the technical details immediately.\n\nTo fix the E15 error and dry out the bottom of your Bosch dishwasher, follow these steps carefully:\n\n1.  **Check the Leak Sensor (Float Switch):** Locate the float switch at the bottom of the tub. It is usually a small plastic arm or cylinder. If it is stuck down or covered in food debris, the sensor thinks there is a flood. Gently lift the float to ensure it moves freely. If it is stuck, you may need to clean the area around it with a soft brush.\n\n2.  **Dry Out the Machine:**\n    *   **Remove the Filter:** Take out the bottom filter and rinse it under warm water to remove any trapped food particles.\n    *   **Open the Door:** Leave the dishwasher door open.\n    *   **Air Dry:** Use a towel to wipe up any standing water, then leave the door open for several hours or overnight to let the interior air dry completely.\n    *   **Run a Drain Cycle:** If you have a \"Rinse\" or \"",
